was rescued when he collapsed in the wild.
在野外倒下后得到了救助。

8
00:00:17,980 --> 00:00:21,880
After a few days in the orphanage in Nairobi,
在内罗毕的孤儿院里待了几天后，

9
00:00:21,880 --> 00:00:24,520
Daphne made a devastating discovery.
达芙妮有了惊人的发现。

10
00:00:24,520 --> 00:00:28,440
- Unfortunately, one eye is blind.
——不幸的是，它的一只眼睛看不见了。

11
00:00:28,440 --> 00:00:30,520
The other one looks like it's getting blind.
另一个看起来快要失明了。

12
00:00:30,520 --> 00:00:36,200
Say we've got a blind elephant.
假设我们有一头失明的大象。

13
00:00:36,200 --> 00:00:40,160
(dramatic music)
（戏剧性音乐）

14
00:00:40,160 --> 00:00:57,680
- We're following the stories of a group
- 我们正在追踪一群

15
00:00:57,680 --> 00:01:00,240
of orphaned baby elephants in Kenya.
肯尼亚孤儿象的故事。

16
00:01:00,240 --> 00:01:01,880
All of them have been rescued by
它们都被

17
00:01:01,880 --> 00:01:04,120
the David Sheldrick Wildlife Trust
大卫·谢尔德里克野生动物基金会救起。

18
00:01:04,120 --> 00:01:07,360
and brought to a unique orphanage in Nairobi.
并被送到了内罗毕一家独特的孤儿院。

19
00:01:07,360 --> 00:01:08,960
Here, they're reared and nurtured
在这里，它们由

20
00:01:08,960 --> 00:01:11,880
